[
  {
    "description": "  Content-scoped policy rules (sovereign-ai-bots #99) let an operator teach\n  Mail Sentinel from the message body or local preview text, not just the\n  sender or subject. #99 extended the #98 `scope` field on the existing\n  `content` policy type with two new values: `body` (matches the full locally\n  parsed message text) and `snippet` (matches `message.snippet`, the first 500\n  chars of the local preview). These scenarios drive a real email with a body\n  marker through the live mailbox and assert that the rule is created locally,\n  shown in the policy listing, and applied during local classification — and\n  that snippet matching is bounded to the 500-char preview window.",
